<GuidePage
  title="Finished Size vs. Cut Size in Quilting"
  guideSlug="finished-vs-cut-size"
  guideCategory="reference"
  description="Understand finished, unfinished, and cut dimensions so seam allowance is added once—and your quilt pieces finish at the intended size."
>
  <section>
    <h2>The three measurements are not interchangeable</h2>
    <dl>
      <dt><strong>Finished size</strong></dt>
      <dd>The visible size after a piece is sewn into the quilt.</dd>
      <dt><strong>Unfinished size</strong></dt>
      <dd>
        The size of a sewn unit before it is joined on all remaining edges.
      </dd>
      <dt><strong>Cut size</strong></dt>
      <dd>The dimensions used to cut the fabric before sewing.</dd>
    </dl>
    <p>
      For a basic rectangle, cut size equals finished size plus seam allowance
      on both opposite edges. With a ¼-inch seam, add ½ inch to both the
      finished width and finished height. A rectangle intended to finish at 3 ×
      6 inches is therefore cut at 3½ × 6½ inches.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Avoid adding seam allowance twice</h2>
    <p>
      Patterns usually say whether a measurement is finished or a cutting
      instruction. If the pattern says “cut 3½ × 6½,” enter it as a cut size;
      those dimensions already contain the allowance. If a design sketch says
      the piece should finish at 3 × 6, enter the finished dimensions and let
      the calculator add the selected seam allowance.
    </p>
    <p>
      Half-square triangles need their method-specific starting-square formula,
      so use the{' '}<a href="/calculators/half-square-triangle/"
        >HST calculator</a
      >{' '}instead of treating them as plain rectangles.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Check the assumption before cutting</h2>
    <p>
      QuiltClarity defaults to a ¼-inch seam, but the field remains editable.
      Confirm the pattern, test your machine’s seam, and keep all inputs in one
      measurement system. Then use the{' '}<a
        href="/calculators/fabric-yardage/">fabric yardage calculator</a
      >{' '}for a repeated piece or review the{' '}<a
        href="/guides/quilt-seam-allowance/">seam allowance guide</a
      >{' '}for the full width-to-finished-size relationship.
    </p>
  </section>
</GuidePage>
